<p>British Prime Minister Keir Starmer is under renewed pressure after Downing Street confirmed that Peter Mandelson was appointed as the United Kingdom’s ambassador to Washington even though he had failed a Cabinet Office security vetting process in 2024. Starmer said it was “staggering” and “unforgivable” that no one told him about the failed vetting before Mandelson took up the post. Opponents said that explanation strains credibility and called for him to resign. The immediate fallout included the dismissal of Olly Robbins, the top civil servant at the Foreign Office, and Starmer’s promise to give Parliament more facts at the start of the next week. The affair has also become a broader test of accountability inside Whitehall, because reporting suggests senior civil servants did not pass the vetting outcome to the prime minister even as Mandelson’s links to Jeffrey Epstein continued to hang over the appointment.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tBTHF_DQ_pAdAO5qIM2whFW4PxD9XiErxNFKj8eVSgXKyKPjl_EOGpnufJPFeQw7UKJ_EpXkJhO95iM1upQwz-jMQTJwpL_Pg6vINF7mU6SbdzPPSESC89lVc7XTzIB7TWwPIuG3mi8e1TVB14dlOIXncaUWTDoCrlQNJsiIBVGyGKhcuGxqwJEtb5i8jC2XNO6mYiqkXRLMsQCwC51uJw' alt='British Prime Minister Keir Starmer in Paris on April 17, 2026, after saying he had not been told Peter Mandelson failed security vetting.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Departmental split: RT, citing Guardian reporting, said the Cabinet Office failed Mandelson in vetting, but the Foreign Office pushed ahead with the Washington appointment anyway.</li><li>Prior assurance: Before Downing Street acknowledged the failed clearance, Starmer told Parliament that “due process” had been followed in Mandelson’s appointment.</li><li>Disclosure dilemma: The Guardian reported that officials spent weeks debating whether highly sensitive material about the affair could be released, turning disclosure itself into part of the controversy.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Keir Starmer: Starmer said the Mandelson episode showed a breakdown in what officials told the prime minister, not a decision he knowingly made after seeing a failed clearance. He said he would return to Parliament with a fuller account while refusing to resign. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/17/starmer-rejects-calls-to-quit-as-pressure-mounts-over-mandelson-vetting'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Kemi Badenoch: The Conservative leader said the government’s claim that Starmer did not know about the vetting failure was not believable and argued that the affair should end his premiership. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638581-starmer-mandelson-uk-epstein/'>RT</a>)</li><li>The civil service: The Guardian reported that the breakdown reached the top of Whitehall, with the head of the civil service among the senior officials who did not brief Starmer. That has put as much focus on the bureaucratic chain of command as on party politics. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/apr/17/keir-starmer-kept-in-dark-peter-mandelson-vetting-two-top-civil-servants'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>The New York Times analysis: The paper said the scandal fits a broader pattern in which Starmer appears to have been blindsided over Mandelson, feeding a narrative that he is not fully in command of the government he leads. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/17/world/europe/starmer-credibility-mandelson-epstein-scandal.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638581-starmer-mandelson-uk-epstein/'>UK PM Starmer accused of ‘blatant dishonesty’ over Epstein-linked envoy</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-uks-starmer-says-staggering-he-was-not-told-of-mandelson-vetting/'>U.K.&#x27;s Starmer says &#x27;staggering&#x27; he was not told of Mandelson vetting failure</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/apr/17/keir-starmer-kept-in-dark-peter-mandelson-vetting-two-to